# Convex Schema Patterns

## Key Differences from Supabase (Relational -> Document)

| Supabase (PostgreSQL)       | Convex (Document DB)                 |
| --------------------------- | ------------------------------------ |
| Foreign keys (`REFERENCES`) | `v.id("tableName")`                  |
| JOINs                       | Multiple queries or denormalization  |
| `uuid` primary key          | `_id` auto-generated by Convex       |
| `created_at TIMESTAMP`      | `_creationTime` built-in (epoch ms)  |
| `updated_at TIMESTAMP`      | Not built-in; add manually if needed |
| Enums (`CREATE TYPE`)       | `v.union(v.literal(...), ...)`       |
| `NULL` columns              | `v.optional(v.type())`               |
| `JSONB` columns             | `v.any()` or typed objects           |
| `integer[]` arrays          | `v.array(v.number())`                |
| Row Level Security          | Access control in function handlers  |

## Schema Conventions

### Table names: camelCase

```typescript
// Convex uses camelCase for table names
gamePlayers; // not game_players
gameSessions; // not game_sessions
joinRequests; // not join_requests
```

### Field names: camelCase

```typescript
// Convex uses camelCase for fields
gameId; // not game_id
hostId; // not host_id
seatNumber; // not seat_number
isAlive; // not is_alive
```

### References between tables

```typescript
// Use v.id("tableName") for references
gamePlayers: defineTable({
  gameId: v.id("games"), // references games table
  playerId: v.id("users"), // references users table (from authTables)
  seatNumber: v.optional(v.number()),
});
```

### Indexes (required for filtered queries)

```typescript
// Always add indexes for fields you query by
gamePlayers: defineTable({
  gameId: v.id("games"),
  playerId: v.id("users"),
})
  .index("by_gameId", ["gameId"])
  .index("by_gameId_playerId", ["gameId", "playerId"]);
```

### Enums as unions

```typescript
// Use v.union with v.literal for enum-like fields
gameStatus: v.union(
  v.literal("not_started"),
  v.literal("playing"),
  v.literal("finished"),
);
```

### Optional fields

```typescript
// Use v.optional() for nullable fields
seatNumber: v.optional(v.number()),    // can be undefined
mafiaTarget: v.optional(v.number()),   // can be undefined
```

### Timestamps

```typescript
// Convex _creationTime is automatic (epoch ms)
// For custom timestamps, use v.number() with Date.now()
speakerStartedAt: v.optional(v.number()),  // epoch ms
foulSpeakStartedAt: v.optional(v.number()),
```

## Querying Patterns

### Get by ID

```typescript
const game = await ctx.db.get(gameId);
```

### Query with index

```typescript
const players = await ctx.db
  .query("gamePlayers")
  .withIndex("by_gameId", (q) => q.eq("gameId", gameId))
  .collect();
```

### Query unique (one-to-one)

```typescript
const session = await ctx.db
  .query("gameSessions")
  .withIndex("by_gameId", (q) => q.eq("gameId", gameId))
  .unique();
```

### Query with compound index

```typescript
const player = await ctx.db
  .query("gamePlayers")
  .withIndex("by_gameId_playerId", (q) =>
    q.eq("gameId", gameId).eq("playerId", userId),
  )
  .unique();
```

## Writing Patterns

### Insert

```typescript
const id = await ctx.db.insert("gamePlayers", {
  gameId,
  playerId: userId,
  seatNumber: 1,
  isAlive: true,
  fouls: 0,
});
```

### Update (patch)

```typescript
await ctx.db.patch(sessionId, {
  gamePhase: "day_phase",
  currentSpeakerIndex: 1,
});
```

### Replace (full overwrite)

```typescript
await ctx.db.replace(sessionId, { ...fullDocument });
```

### Delete

```typescript
await ctx.db.delete(requestId);
```

## Type Usage

```typescript
import { Doc, Id } from "@/convex/_generated/dataModel";

// Document type (full row)
type Game = Doc<"games">;

// ID type
type GameId = Id<"games">;

// In function args
args: {
  gameId: v.id("games");
}
// TypeScript infers: { gameId: Id<"games"> }
```

## Migration Notes (Supabase -> Convex)

- `Tables<"games">` becomes `Doc<"games">`
- `string` UUIDs become `Id<"games">` (Convex IDs)
- `created_at: string` becomes `_creationTime: number` (automatic)
- `game_id` field becomes `gameId` (camelCase)
- Foreign key lookups become `ctx.db.get(id)` calls
- No JOINs: fetch related data with separate queries in the same handler
